1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:00,990
Here's a word you'll

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:02,440
see in business news.

3
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:03,320
Opaque.

4
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,520
oh-PAYK.

5
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:06,580
Stress on the second syllable.

6
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:09,240
Opaque means you can't see through it:

7
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:10,760
hard to understand.

8
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,550
For example,

9
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:15,560
"The company's finances remain opaque to investors."

10
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,720
The opposite is transparent.

11
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,510
At work,

12
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:19,230
try:

13
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:21,250
"This process is a little opaque."

14
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:24,760
Comment NEXT for the next word.

15
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,860
Follow The Fluent Edge for more.
